00:06:22,500 --> 00:06:28,500
Free your mind.

2
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:51,000
The Animatrix is a animation, science fiction film directed by Peter Chung.

3
00:19:07,500 --> 00:19:13,500
Straight from the creators of the groundbreaking Matrix trilogy, this collection of short animated films from the world's leading anime directors
fuses computer graphics and Japanese anime to provide the background of the Matrix universe and the conflict between man and machines.

4
00:25:30,000 --> 00:25:36,000
The shorts include Final Flight of the Osiris, The Second Renaissance, Kid's Story,
Program, World Record, Beyond, A Detective Story and Matriculated.

5
00:31:52,500 --> 00:31:58,500
Neo ("Kid's Story") (voice), played by Keanu Reeves.

6
00:38:15,000 --> 00:38:21,000
Trinity ("Kid's Story" and "A Detective Story")
(voice), played by Carrie-Anne Moss.

7
00:44:37,500 --> 00:44:43,500
The Kid ("Kid's Story") (voice), played by Clayton Watson.

8
00:51:00,000 --> 00:51:06,000
Jue ("Final Flight of the Osiris") / Manabu
("Beyond") (voice), played by Pamela Adlon.

9
00:57:22,500 --> 00:57:28,500
Alexa ("Matriculated") (voice), played by Melinda Clarke.

10
01:03:45,000 --> 01:03:51,000
Crew Man ("Final Flight of the Osiris") / Kaiser
("Program") (voice), played by John DiMaggio.

11
01:10:07,500 --> 01:10:13,500
The Animatrix (Japanese: アニマトリックス, Hepburn: Animatorikkusu) is a 2003 adult
animated science fiction anthology film produced by the Wachowskis.

12
01:16:30,000 --> 01:16:36,000
The anime compiles nine animated short films, detailing the backstory of The Matrix film series, in
addition to providing side stories that expand the universe and tie into the film series.

13
01:22:52,500 --> 01:22:58,500
The film received generally positive reviews from critics and fans.

14
01:29:15,000 --> 01:29:21,000
The film explores themes of martial arts, artificial
intelligence (a.i.), hacker, virtual reality, dystopia.

15
01:35:37,500 --> 01:35:43,500
The tone is thought_provoking.
